# WebClaude group scripts

## Alignment with Claude Code (official)

- Anthropic Claude Code docs: https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/best-practices  
- Hooks (when scripts are used as hooks): https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks-guide  
- Give agents **verifiable success criteria** (e.g. artifact checks), not only “it ran”.

## Repository rules (this tree)

- **Language**: comments, logs, and user-facing strings in **English** only. No emoji in scripts.
- **Variables**: declare **constants and mode flags at the top** of each script (after `param` / option parsing blocks where those must read `$@` first). Path variables may be assigned immediately after parsing if they depend on `BASH_SOURCE` / `$MyInvocation`.
- **Live output**: long-running commands (`npm install`, `pnpm install`, `go build`, `go mod download`, installers) must print to the terminal **in real time**. Do not pipe them through `tail`, `grep` silencers, or capture-only `$()` when the user needs to see progress.
- **Success checks**: prefer **artifact checks** (`test -f` / `Test-Path` for binaries, `node_modules`, etc.) instead of treating exit codes as the primary contract.
- **Privileged Linux commands**: use **`sudo`** for package managers and system services when not running as root (e.g. `apt-get`, `systemctl` where appropriate).
- **Sourcing**: **trust-style** includes — `source` expected library paths **without** redundant `if [[ -f ... ]]` guards. Missing files should fail fast in a complete checkout.
- **Text / env parsing**: avoid complex `grep`/`sed`/`tail` pipelines in shell for structured data. Helpers under `webclaude_group/scripts/pytools/`:
  - **`wc_env.py`**: read a key from an env-style file.
  - **`wc_line_value.py`**: first `KEY=value` assignment in a file (e.g. gvar-style lines).
  - **`wc_list_backups.py`**: list last N glob matches in a directory (replaces `ls … | tail`).
  - **`wc_tail_file.py`**: print last N lines of a file (replaces `tail -n` in scripts).
- **Documentation**: do not generate large markdown from shell; keep scripts thin.
- **Exit status**: launcher utilities may end with **`exit 0`** so callers do not rely on exit codes; infer outcome from `[OK]` / `[FAIL]` lines and filesystem artifacts. (This does **not** apply to Claude Code hook scripts.)
- **Backlog**: `webclaude_center_server/scripts/manage.sh` still contains extensive non-English strings outside the paths already migrated; translate incrementally when touching that file.

## Note on hook scripts (if reused under `.claude/`)

Claude Code hook handlers use specific exit codes per Anthropic hook documentation. Repository launcher scripts under `webclaude_group/` are **not** hook handlers unless installed as such; rules above apply to these launchers.
